<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-dionaea-muscipula-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Dionaea muscipula Turing wavenumber at 24 µm (pass 2) (Dionaea muscipula)",
        "Dionaea muscipula Turing wavenumber at 24 µm (pass 2) faithfully reproduces Dionaea muscipula morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-dionaea-muscipula-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-dionaea-muscipula-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-dionaea-muscipula-turing-wavelength-s0-3> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-dionaea-muscipula-turing-wavelength-s0.py, docs/media/dionaea_muscipula_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png, datasets/dionaea_muscipula_turing_wavelength_s0/metrics.json implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Dionaea muscipula specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/datasets/dionaea_muscipula_turing_wavelength_s0/metrics.json>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/docs/media/dionaea_muscipula_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-dionaea-muscipula-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Dionaea muscipula" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: A published wet-lab spacing of 24.00 µm for Dionaea digestive glands.",
        "does_not_claim: A second independent assessor.",
        "does_not_claim: That the redness KS of 0.008 validates the PDE against gland positions. It only says the last frame is close to the photograph.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Du and Dv at ratio 18 so that λ_c = 24 µm exactly.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Fourier PDE, pure-mode growth rates, diffusivity sweep, and Dv = Du ablation.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Otsu redness segmentation of the Wikimedia specimen and of the GIF last frame.",
        "reported_in_source: Forterre 2005 and Hedrich & Neher 2018 describe the trap lobe. They do not measure a 24 µm pigment wavelength.",
        "reported_in_source: Murray 1981: the number of wavelengths that fit changes when the domain grows and the intrinsic wavelength does not.",
        "reported_in_source: Schnakenberg 1979 supplies the kinetics a − u + u²v and b − u²v.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing 1952 selects a finite k_c from the dispersion relation of a two-species reaction-diffusion system.",
        "transfer_boundary: 24 µm is the assigned cellular-detail scale. Age is 0 Ma. Chronoseries length is 1.",
        "transfer_boundary: Marginal cilia and the lobe outline in the GIF are taken from the photograph. The PDE grows the activator on a flat patch; it does not grow the cilia.",
        "transfer_boundary: The saturated wavelength is 1.25 times the linear k_c, not equal to it. RMSE of that sweep is 7.47 µm." ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-dionaea-muscipula-turing-wavelength-s0.py, https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/docs/media/dionaea_muscipula_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png, https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/datasets/dionaea_muscipula_turing_wavelength_s0/metrics.json; output: docs/media/dionaea_muscipula_turing_wavelength_s0_growth.gif; organism: Dionaea muscipula; environment: n/a; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing 1952 selects a finite k_c from the dispersion relation of a two-species reaction-diffusion system. | Schnakenberg 1979 supplies the kinetics a − u + u²v and b − u²v. | Murray 1981: the number of wavelengths that fit changes when the domain grows and the intrinsic wavelength does not. | Forterre 2005 and Hedrich & Neher 2018 describe the trap lobe. They do not measure a 24 µm pigment wavelength.; reconstructed_in_script: Du and Dv at ratio 18 so that λ_c = 24 µm exactly. | Fourier PDE, pure-mode growth rates, diffusivity sweep, and Dv = Du ablation. | Otsu redness segmentation of the Wikimedia specimen and of the GIF last frame.; transfer_boundary: Marginal cilia and the lobe outline in the GIF are taken from the photograph. The PDE grows the activator on a flat patch; it does not grow the cilia. | The saturated wavelength is 1.25 times the linear k_c, not equal to it. RMSE of that sweep is 7.47 µm. | 24 µm is the assigned cellular-detail scale. Age is 0 Ma. Chronoseries length is 1.; does_not_claim: A published wet-lab spacing of 24.00 µm for Dionaea digestive glands. | That the redness KS of 0.008 validates the PDE against gland positions. It only says the last frame is close to the photograph. | A second independent assessor.]; phenomenon_size: 6.1 mm (0.006138 m, log10=-2.212 m, tier=6_organ_mm); species_scale_ladder (1 runs from 6.1 mm to 6.1 mm): 6.1 mm:venus-flytrap-snap-buckling" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(79)90042-0>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(81)90334-9>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.tplants.2017.12.004>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature03185>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1952.0012>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1179047> ;
    pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-dionaea-muscipula-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-dionaea-muscipula-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity>,
