<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-dionaea-muscipula-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Dionaea muscipula Turing wavenumber at 24 µm (pass 2) — Code-to-model traceability: 84/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "sigma_analytic is the dispersion formula from the docstring. The Lean file proves the integer shadow of the margin, the trace, the ablation sign, and the 8 / 20 wavelength counts. Pass-2 plotting labels the numeric curve against that formula." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-dionaea-muscipula-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-dionaea-muscipula-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.4e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-dionaea-muscipula-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Dionaea muscipula Turing wavenumber at 24 µm (pass 2) — Model fidelity to source: 88/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The script integrates Schnakenberg kinetics and compares pure-mode PDE growth to the Turing eigenvalue. Pearson r is 0.999999 and RMSE is 0.00137. a = 0.10 and b = 0.90 are chosen so the slot wavelength is 24 µm; they are not Dionaea-specific constants from Schnakenberg 1979." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-dionaea-muscipula-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-dionaea-muscipula-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-dionaea-muscipula-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Dionaea muscipula Turing wavenumber at 24 µm (pass 2) — Morphometric validation: 84/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Dispersion Pearson r = 0.999999 (reference gate 0.98) and RMSE = 0.00137 (reference 0). The sweep RMSE is 7.47 µm because saturated spots run at 1.25 times the linear wavelength; that bias is reported. Specimen foreground 0.449 vs render 0.445, coherency 0.475 vs 0.474, circularity 0.0167 vs 0.0169, redness KS 0.0083 vs a null of 0. The KS is small because the frame is built on the photograph." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
