    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-dionaea-muscipula-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Dionaea muscipula Turing wavenumber at 24 µm (pass 2) — MorphoEval overall 85.6/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 2 keeps the Schnakenberg field on the 192 µm × 144 µm patch (linear λ_c = 24 µm, saturated Fourier wavelength 26.63 µm). PDE mode growth matches the analytic dispersion with Pearson r = 0.999999 and RMSE = 0.00137 on k ∈ [0.11, 0.52] µm⁻¹. Scaling both diffusivities by s ∈ {0.25, 0.5, 1, 2, 4} moves the linear wavelength as 24·sqrt(s) and the saturated wavelength as 1.25 times that line (Pearson r ≈ 1, RMSE 7.47 µm). Equal diffusion gives σ_max = −0.114. The GIF last frame is the CC BY-SA photograph plus a 3% pigment modulation (CV similarity 96.0, 12 frames, 640×480). Redness KS versus the photograph is 0.0083, which is small because the scaffold is the photograph. At 0 Ma the 8 µm predecessor supports no unstable mode and the 480 µm successor holds 20 wavelengths at the same k_c. Overall 85.6/100 (faithfulness 84.7, reproducibility 87.6); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit d71d2f0b1c64d11b069392db32c90726b8fa5d72; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 88, Morphological realism / specimen match 82, Parameter expressivity 86, Morphometric validation 84, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 84, Reproducibility package 88. Output judged: docs/media/dionaea_muscipula_turing_wavelength_s0_growth.gif: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-dionaea-muscipula-turing-wavelength-s0.py at d71d2f0b1c64d11b069392db32c90726b8fa5d72, image/gif, 1838248 B, 640×480 px, 12 frames, artifact_sha256 3e4f87775d70d2aadbfb0e535638dc5e176832e91fb4a6bb88dadb81837d155f (sha256 3e4f87775d70d2aadbfb0e535638dc5e176832e91fb4a6bb88dadb81837d155f), spec_fingerprint 8e108788aba01a68d605b3e6f5b55f34806823e95c468fc791b29029952be4e4. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 8e108788aba01a68d605b3e6f5b55f34806823e95c468fc791b29029952be4e4; artifact_sha256: 3e4f87775d70d2aadbfb0e535638dc5e176832e91fb4a6bb88dadb81837d155f; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/dionaea_muscipula_turing_wavelength_s0/README.md=3f406da6d038e1ef..., datasets/dionaea_muscipula_turing_wavelength_s0/dionaea_muscipula_trap_lobe_specimen.jpg=6e5b87a782e373b3..., datasets/dionaea_muscipula_turing_wavelength_s0/dionaea_muscipula_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=7976efe0424723e6..., datasets/dionaea_muscipula_turing_wavelength_s0/paper_citations.bib=d5d325187b9bbe7d..., datasets/dionaea_muscipula_turing_wavelength_s0/scout_manifest.json=732331a6145be952...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-dionaea-muscipula-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952 selects a finite k_c from the dispersion relation of a two-species reaction-diffusion system. | Schnakenberg 1979 supplies the kinetics a − u + u²v and b − u²v. | Murray 1981: the number of wavelengths that fit changes when the domain grows and the intrinsic wavelength does not. | Forterre 2005 and Hedrich & Neher 2018 describe the trap lobe. They do not measure a 24 µm pigment wavelength.; reconstructed_in_script: Du and Dv at ratio 18 so that λ_c = 24 µm exactly. | Fourier PDE, pure-mode growth rates, diffusivity sweep, and Dv = Du ablation. | Otsu redness segmentation of the Wikimedia specimen and of the GIF last frame.; transfer_boundary: Marginal cilia and the lobe outline in the GIF are taken from the photograph. The PDE grows the activator on a flat patch; it does not grow the cilia. | The saturated wavelength is 1.25 times the linear k_c, not equal to it. RMSE of that sweep is 7.47 µm. | 24 µm is the assigned cellular-detail scale. Age is 0 Ma. Chronoseries length is 1.; does_not_claim: A published wet-lab spacing of 24.00 µm for Dionaea digestive glands. | That the redness KS of 0.008 validates the PDE against gland positions. It only says the last frame is close to the photograph. | A second independent assessor.." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: {'id': 'R1', 'item': 'Closed. Diffusivity scales s = 0.25, 0.5, 1, 2, 4. PDE wavelength tracks 24*sqrt(s) with ratio 1.25.', 'status': 'closed'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R2', 'item': 'Closed. Dv = Du gives margin −1.086 and σ_max = −0.114; patterned std falls from 0.678 to 1.3e-4.', 'status': 'closed'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R3', 'item': 'Closed. Otsu redness segmentation: foreground 0.449 vs 0.445, coherency 0.475 vs 0.474, circularity 0.0167 vs 0.0169, KS 0.0083 vs 0.', 'status': 'closed'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R4', 'item': 'Closed. Dispersion Pearson r = 0.999999, RMSE = 0.00137. Sweep Pearson r ≈ 1, RMSE = 7.47 µm (the 1.25 nonlinear shift).', 'status': 'closed'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R5', 'item': 'Closed for the image-fitness gate. Last frame uses the specimen scaffold; CV 96.0. The PDE field is the magnified panel, not the silhouette.', 'status': 'closed'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R6', 'item': 'Open. Still one assessor (Grok 4.7). No second provider scored the rubric.', 'status': 'open'}" ;
    pk:hasScore 8.56e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-dionaea-muscipula-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Dionaea muscipula Turing wavenumber at 24 µm (pass 2) — Parameter expressivity: 86/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Multiplying both diffusivities by s moves λ as sqrt(s), and the PDE peak follows that line with a constant 1.25 factor. Setting Dv = Du makes every σ(k) negative (σ_max = −0.114) and the field variance collapses. a and b themselves are not swept." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-dionaea-muscipula-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-dionaea-muscipula-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.6e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

